INSERT INTO `faqs` VALUES ('faq-1','When should I start preparing my study abroad applications?','We strongly recommend beginning your preparation 10 to 14 months prior to your intended intake. For example, for a September/Fall intake, you should start university shortlisting, English test preparation (IELTS/TOEFL/PTE), and drafting your Statement of Purpose (SOP) by October to December of the previous year. Most top-tier universities open applications in September/October and begin offering places on a rolling basis.','Admissions',1,1,'2026-10-04 18:26:17','2026-10-04 18:26:17'),('faq-10','How do you help me choose the right university?','We deploy a scientific matching methodology evaluating your academic GPA, test scores, target specialization, career aspirations, budgetary boundaries, and post-study work visa ambitions. We construct a balanced portfolio of 6 to 10 universities categorized into \"Dream\" (ambitious top-tier), \"Target\" (strong alignment), and \"Safe\" (guaranteed admission and scholarship likelihood) tiers.','Universities',10,1,'2026-10-04 18:26:17','2026-10-04 18:26:17'),('faq-11','Do you help students find housing before they travel?','Absolutely. We partner with the worldâ€™s leading Purpose-Built Student Accommodation (PBSA) providersâ€”including AmberStudent, Student.com, and Unite Studentsâ€”to help you compare, tour virtually, and legally secure private studios, ensuite apartments, or university on-campus halls with zero booking fees and student cancellation protections.','Accommodation',11,1,'2026-10-04 18:26:17','2026-10-04 18:26:17'),('faq-12','Can I apply if my final year university results are still pending?','Yes! You can apply with your 5th or 6th semester provisional transcripts. Universities will issue a \"Conditional Offer Letter\" securing your seat. Once your final semester marks and degree certificate are published, your offer converts into an Unconditional Offer Letter, allowing you to proceed with your CAS/I-20 and visa application.','Applications',12,1,'2026-10-04 18:26:17','2026-10-04 18:26:17'),('faq-2','Can I apply for a Masterâ€™s degree if I have a 3-year Bachelorâ€™s degree?','Yes! In the UK, Australia, Ireland, and New Zealand, a 3-year Bachelorâ€™s degree (such as BA, BSc, BCom, or BBA) from a recognized university is directly accepted for Masterâ€™s programs. For the USA and Canada, while traditional universities traditionally required 16 years of education (4-year degree), hundreds of leading institutions now accept 3-year degrees evaluated by WES (World Education Services) with high NAAC grade accreditations.','Admissions',2,1,'2026-10-04 18:26:17','2026-10-04 18:26:17'),('faq-3','What is your visa success rate and how do you ensure high approval?','AuraGlobal maintains an audited 98.6% visa success rate across 20+ countries. We achieve this through meticulous document indexing: we verify that financial assets comply precisely with embassy regulations (such as UKVI 28-day holding rules, German Blocked Accounts, and US liquid funds), conduct rigorous 1-on-1 mock interviews simulating real visa officer queries, and draft airtight Statements of Purpose for visas that clearly prove non-immigrant intent.','Visa',3,1,'2026-10-04 18:26:17','2026-10-04 18:26:17'),('faq-4','How much money do I need to show in my bank account for a student visa?','This varies strictly by destination: For the UK, you must show remaining first-year tuition plus 9 months of living expenses (Â£12,006 outside London, Â£14,805 inside London) held continuously in a verified bank account for at least 28 consecutive days. For the USA, you need liquid funds covering the first full year listed on your I-20 (typically $35,000â€“$65,000). For Germany, you must deposit the statutory blocked amount (â‚¬11,904). Our financial advisory team gives you exact, tailored checklists.','Visa',4,1,'2026-10-04 18:26:17','2026-10-04 18:26:17'),('faq-5','Are full-ride scholarships available for international students?','Yes, full-ride scholarships exist through several avenues: government programs like Chevening (UK), Fulbright (USA), DAAD (Germany), and Australia Awards cover 100% of tuition plus monthly living allowances and airfare. Additionally, top US universities offer need-blind financial aid covering 100% of demonstrated financial need. For STEM graduate students, Research Assistantships (RA) and Teaching Assistantships (TA) frequently provide full tuition waivers plus monthly stipends.','Scholarships',5,1,'2026-10-04 18:26:17','2026-10-04 18:26:17'),('faq-6','Does AuraGlobal charge an extra fee to assist with scholarship applications?','No. Comprehensive scholarship guidance and essay alignment are integrated directly into our core advisory packages. We actively identify every institutional bursary, merit award, and competitive grant you are eligible for as part of your application strategy.','Scholarships',6,1,'2026-10-04 18:26:17','2026-10-04 18:26:17'),('faq-7','Can I study abroad without IELTS or TOEFL?','Yes, in several circumstances! Many UK, Australian, and European universities grant English Language Proficiency Waivers if you scored 70%+ in High School English (CBSE/ISC/State Boards) or completed your previous degree at an institution where the medium of instruction (MOI) was English. Duolingo English Test (DET) and PTE Academic are also widely accepted alternative computerized exams.','IELTS',7,1,'2026-10-04 18:26:17','2026-10-04 18:26:17'),('faq-8','What is the minimum IELTS score required for top universities?','Most leading universities require an overall IELTS Academic band score of 6.5 with no individual band below 6.0 for Masterâ€™s programs. Highly competitive institutions like Oxford, Cambridge, Imperial, Harvard, and Columbia typically demand Band 7.0 to 7.5 with minimum 6.5 or 7.0 in each sub-component (Listening, Reading, Writing, Speaking).','IELTS',8,1,'2026-10-04 18:26:17','2026-10-04 18:26:17'),('faq-9','What are your consultancy charges for students?','Our initial comprehensive profile assessment and strategy consultation are 100% FREE. For standard partner university applications across the UK, Australia, Canada, and Europe, our core admission processing is completely free of charge as we are officially funded university representatives. For bespoke Ivy League, Oxbridge, and elite PhD/Scholarship coaching, we offer transparent, flat-fee premium mentoring packages with zero hidden costs.','Fees',9,1,'2026-10-04 18:26:17','2026-10-04 18:26:17');
/*!40000 ALTER TABLE `faqs` ENABLE KEYS */;
UNLOCK TABLES;

